WEBVTT

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:05.770
ONE YEAR AGO

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:05.350
Hang in there, Sun-chan.

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:08.020
You want to encourage this person.

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:10.230
Is that the name of someone dear to you?

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:12.530
That's right.

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:17.530
Unlike me,
he's heading in the direction of his dreams.

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:24.580
So right now I'm sure he's really frustrated
about losing the game.

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:28.380
I was thinking, at a time like this,
if there's anything I can do...

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:29.840
I see.

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:32.260
Oh.

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:36.260
CHEERFUL SKEWER STAND

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:36.260
It's just that I was surprised
when you suddenly came running over

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:39.720
and said, "Please give me
all of your deep-fried skewers."

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:43.390
Sorry for the unreasonable demand.

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:45.190
No, not at all.

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:50.940
I've hardly had any customers today,
so for me, you're like a blessing.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:53.940
Besides, you encouraged me, too.

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:55.860
I did?

00:00:56.990 --> 00:01:02.040
If there's somebody like you, who busts
his tail to do his best for someone else,

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:05.370
then maybe I'll try a little harder, too.

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:07.750
Thank you.

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:10.540
What does that mean?

00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:13.300
All right. This makes all of them.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:16.760
- They're really hot, so be careful.
- I will.

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:19.140
Well, I'll be on my way.

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:21.310
Okay. Thank you!

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:22.430
No, thank you!

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:25.940
Wait!

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:27.350
Yes?

00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:32.530
Listen, if you don't mind,
would you tell me your name?

00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:34.490
Me?

00:01:35.570 --> 00:01:36.990
My name is...

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:14.170
EPISODE 08
BEFORE I KNEW IT,
MY TRAGEDY
HAD ALREADY BEGUN

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:17.670
From now on, I'll do everything I can for you
with all my heart, so please be kind.

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:24.300
Hey, that's kind of a lousy attitude.

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:26.180
Well, after all...

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:28.770
Touching one's lips to the back of the hand

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:33.190
of the person you're devoted to as a display
of will is only normal, so that was odd.

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:35.520
<i>What am I, a nobleman?</i>

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:38.530
Um, Yoki...

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:40.570
would you introduce yourself now?

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:42.240
Oh, that's right.

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:44.240
Well, Amatsuyu Kisaragi...

00:03:44.570 --> 00:03:45.570
I'll talk to you later.

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:47.620
Yo!

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:50.330
I'm Chiharu Yoki.

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:51.580
At my old school,

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:56.040
they called me Tsubaki, from
the second characters of my first and last names.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:58.000
My family runs
a deep-fried skewer shop

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:01.130
and just opened a second one,
so we moved near here.

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:06.140
The name of the place is Cheerful Skewers,
because that's what my last name means.

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:08.680
<i>Deep-fried skewer shop...</i>

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:09.890
Don't tell me.

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:11.930
The girl from that day!

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:14.900
Maybe you finally remembered?

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:18.900
Cheerful Skewers, you say?

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:22.240
Deep-fried crispiness!
The harmony of coating and crunchiness...

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:26.030
that spreads with every bite!

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:31.250
The emerald-green torrent that runs
just by licking it is the Aegean Sea of sauces!

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:29.870
NO DOUBLE DIPPING
IN THE SAUCE

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:34.000
Aside from the taste, it heals my soul!

00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:40.590
Is it that Cheerful Skewers
with the ultimate, supreme skewers?!

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:43.380
I think we're that one.

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:46.300
<i>One what now?</i>

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:47.680
<i>Anyway...</i>

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:51.390
<i>Even though it was on the back of my hand,</i>

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:54.480
<i>suddenly kissing a guy
on your first day at a new school</i>

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:57.060
<i>might leave you ostracized in class.
Will you be okay?</i>

00:04:57.770 --> 00:04:58.900
I don't believe it!

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:02.490
So you already knew her!

00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:10.240
How can he let her do that when I'm here?

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:12.750
I'm going to tell Pansy and Cosmos.

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:17.880
<i>I'm used to being ostracized at school,
so it's no problem for me.</i>

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:20.040
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:21.920
I see!

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:26.510
That's what happened
between you and Joro, then!

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:33.640
So I intend to pay Amatsuyu Kisaragi back
and then some for helping me out.

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:35.180
Good job, Joro!

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:36.230
Ow!

00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:38.230
I-It just happened that way.

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:42.230
<i>How long is that baseball game singularity
going to run rampant?</i>

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:45.070
Unbelievable.

00:05:45.490 --> 00:05:46.900
What?

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:50.320
Maybe you want to devote yourself
to Amatsuyu Kisaragi, too?

00:05:50.990 --> 00:05:52.830
O-Of course not!

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:54.950
Devote myself? It's the last thing I'd do!

00:05:54.950 --> 00:05:57.500
I see. Maybe I misread it.

00:05:57.750 --> 00:06:02.380
D-Damn right you did!
In the first place, I have zero interest in him!

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:05.630
On top of that, he isn't interested in me! Right?

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:06.590
R-Right.

00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:07.760
Why aren't you interested?

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:08.630
Sorry.

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:11.970
Amatsuyu Kisaragi.

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:16.480
I'll do anything for you.

00:06:16.480 --> 00:06:19.310
So don't hold back. Say anything.

00:06:23.020 --> 00:06:25.860
Well, there isn't anything
I especially want you to do.

00:06:26.650 --> 00:06:30.950
For example, you could say,
"I'm being stalked, so help me out."

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:33.530
Or "I'm afraid someone is reading my mind."

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:34.580
Nothing like that?

00:06:34.910 --> 00:06:36.790
Let's stick to sensible things.

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:41.380
There's no high school student
who's in a situation like that.

00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:43.380
I guess you're right.

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:45.420
All right, everyone. Take your seats.

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:48.760
Well, if you think of anything,
let me know any time.

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:48.220
We're starting class.

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:51.220
Amatsuyu Kisaragi.

00:06:53.140 --> 00:06:54.640
S-Sure.

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:04.230
So by coincidence,
I met the new girl in school once before,

00:07:04.230 --> 00:07:08.320
and, as fate would have it,
she's now in my class.

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:11.610
Plus she's devoted to serving me
without any compensation.

00:07:13.780 --> 00:07:18.700
As if a convenient woman like that
actually exists in this world!

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:24.210
I dare say that woman, Tsubaki,
is definitely up to something!

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:27.000
But don't think
you can manipulate me so easily.

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:32.430
I'll reveal your true colors
and crush your plot until nothing is left!

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:38.720
I got a little worked up there,
but this has been Amatsuyu Kisaragi.

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:42.940
Kisaragi! After class, put away these materials.

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:47.650
MATERIALS

00:07:44.310 --> 00:07:46.650
- The files go on that shelf.
- Okay.

00:07:47.150 --> 00:07:49.360
Sorry about asking you to help.

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:52.030
This is a cinch!

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:57.490
<i>Now how am I going to expose
her fiendish true nature?</i>

00:07:57.990 --> 00:07:58.830
Hey.

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:02.370
I'd like to call you Joro, too.

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:03.540
Is that okay?

00:08:03.870 --> 00:08:05.290
<i>This woman!</i>

00:08:05.290 --> 00:08:08.550
<i>Her shameless flirting
permeates every fiber of her being!</i>

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:10.670
Sure. I don't mind.

00:08:12.170 --> 00:08:13.180
Great!

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:14.550
Well, shall we go back?

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:17.680
<i>The sly vixen!</i>

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:20.810
Look out! Joro!

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:24.810
Don't go there.

00:08:24.810 --> 00:08:26.060
G-Go where?

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:26.900
There.

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:30.990
I don't know why, but there's
a banana peel on the floor.

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:35.240
If you step on it,
you might slip, fall, and injure yourself.

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:40.240
What is it?

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:43.120
<i>Danger!</i>

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:44.830
<i>What an innocent smile...</i>

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:45.830
<i>not!</i>

00:08:45.830 --> 00:08:47.380
<i>It's a shady smile!</i>

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:49.750
<i>Anybody else would have fallen for her act!</i>

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:52.170
Th-Thank you!

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:54.090
Listen.

00:08:55.010 --> 00:09:00.180
If you don't mind, would you like
to eat the lunch I made today?

00:09:00.470 --> 00:09:03.270
Just in case, I prepared an extra one.

00:09:03.270 --> 00:09:06.310
<i>Why didn't she make her debut
in the first episode?</i>

00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:07.860
Thank you.

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:10.520
I didn't bring lunch today,
so that would be a big help.

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:12.230
Great!

00:09:14.650 --> 00:09:17.740
<i>Don't be fooled! This is a trap!
She must have some other purpose!</i>

00:09:17.740 --> 00:09:18.910
<i>I-I've got it!</i>

00:09:19.330 --> 00:09:23.000
You know, I'm feeling guilty
having you do everything for me,

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:26.670
so isn't there something I can do for you?

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:28.750
- Something for me?
- Yeah.

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:33.710
Something hard to ask of anyone else.
Something you can only ask me to do.

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:36.680
<i>Okay, expose everything!</i>

00:09:37.010 --> 00:09:42.010
<i>The true character of a rotten woman
who can't help but use men!</i>

00:09:43.140 --> 00:09:43.970
Well...

00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:47.480
I'd like you to let me
continue to serve you from now on.

00:09:47.480 --> 00:09:51.150
If you're pleased, then I'm delighted!

00:09:57.070 --> 00:09:59.740
<i>Fine. If she's deceiving me, so be it.</i>

00:09:59.740 --> 00:10:00.990
<i>After all...</i>

00:10:00.990 --> 00:10:05.040
<i>If you're pleased, then I'm delighted!</i>

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:08.960
<i>She's a super-authentic main heroine!</i>

00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:13.710
LIBRARY

00:10:13.210 --> 00:10:17.720
I'm Chiharu Yoki,
and it's my first day in Joro's class.

00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:20.050
Please call me Tsubaki.

00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:23.430
It's nice to meet you, Cosmos, Pansy.

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:25.470
Yes, likewise.

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:28.190
By the way, how did you know our names?

00:10:29.190 --> 00:10:30.650
I told her!

00:10:30.650 --> 00:10:33.270
I said you're my dear friends!

00:10:33.270 --> 00:10:34.360
Oh.

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:38.360
I see. It's a pleasure to meet you too, Tsubaki.

00:10:38.490 --> 00:10:41.030
Well, let's all have lunch together!

00:10:41.030 --> 00:10:41.870
All right!

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:43.950
Lunch! Lunch!

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:45.330
Lunch. R-Right. Yeah!

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:47.080
Lunch.

00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:48.660
Thank you for the food!

00:10:56.130 --> 00:10:58.170
Sun-chan, you're a glutton!

00:10:57.630 --> 00:10:58.510
<i>All right, now!</i>

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:00.260
Joro! If you like—

00:11:00.260 --> 00:11:02.890
Here you go, Joro!
As promised, my homemade lunch!

00:11:05.970 --> 00:11:07.470
Thank you, Tsuba...

00:11:09.350 --> 00:11:11.650
What's that, President Cosmos?

00:11:12.020 --> 00:11:14.270
V-Verily, it is nothing.

00:11:14.270 --> 00:11:17.190
Indeed, I just happened to bring
a few whatnots from home,

00:11:17.190 --> 00:11:19.320
but I definitely did not mean to feed Joro...

00:11:20.650 --> 00:11:21.910
Oh, my gosh!

00:11:21.910 --> 00:11:24.120
A luxo-quadruple-decker boxed lunch!

00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:26.660
Th-This is no problem, verily!

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:29.330
Why, I am into fasting of late!

00:11:29.580 --> 00:11:31.790
<i>Isn't that a wacky way to fast?</i>

00:11:33.290 --> 00:11:36.170
This is the biggest blunder of my life.

00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:37.670
Um, President Cosmos...

00:11:38.050 --> 00:11:41.010
since you've got it here,
do you mind if I have some?

00:11:41.010 --> 00:11:42.090
What?

00:11:42.090 --> 00:11:44.510
Is that the eternal truth, devoid of falsehoods?

00:11:45.050 --> 00:11:48.020
I-It's the eternal truth, devoid of falsehoods!

00:11:49.980 --> 00:11:53.230
<i>I have no regrets in this life!</i>

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:57.360
What?

00:11:57.360 --> 00:11:59.070
I'm glad you were able to make an excuse.

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:02.780
Yay!

00:12:06.370 --> 00:12:07.280
Delicious!

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:10.000
Your cookies are always delicious, Pansy!

00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:12.210
Thank you.

00:12:12.210 --> 00:12:13.620
I can't eat another bite.

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:18.920
Yum!

00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:19.960
I know, right?

00:12:23.340 --> 00:12:25.590
Huh? Himawari, what's with the racket?

00:12:26.890 --> 00:12:27.850
Um...

00:12:28.140 --> 00:12:33.100
This racket is getting old,
so I was thinking about buying a new one.

00:12:33.350 --> 00:12:36.440
It took me a long time,
but I saved up my allowance for it!

00:12:36.650 --> 00:12:41.280
I, uh, just wanted to know
why you brought it to the library.

00:12:41.530 --> 00:12:46.570
We've got a tournament coming up,
so I'm ready to practice anytime, anywhere!

00:12:46.570 --> 00:12:48.910
I'll do my best
for the interscholastic athletic meet!

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:53.040
Nice! As for me, the team's definitely
going to make Koshien this year!

00:12:53.830 --> 00:12:56.420
I've prepared a secret weapon.

00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:58.880
You both sound promising.

00:12:58.880 --> 00:13:02.380
As the president of student council,
I'll organize a cheering squad

00:13:02.380 --> 00:13:05.380
and coordinate schedules,
so you two just do your best.

00:13:05.380 --> 00:13:07.090
- Sure!
- Yeah!

00:13:08.600 --> 00:13:11.970
Come to think of it,
are you good at something, Joro?

00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:15.190
No, not especially.

00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:18.650
I see. Then I'm sure
you'll acquire some skill here on out.

00:13:23.780 --> 00:13:28.660
So what did you want to talk about?
You had just me stay behind.

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:31.830
So you know,
I have no intention of talking about Tsubaki.

00:13:32.290 --> 00:13:34.210
Finally, a kind angel has come to me—

00:13:34.210 --> 00:13:36.920
I actually don't have any complaints
about her behavior.

00:13:37.170 --> 00:13:42.340
After all, I can understand something like
paying someone back for their help.

00:13:42.960 --> 00:13:44.420
Then, what do you—

00:13:44.420 --> 00:13:48.340
My problem is with a certain coward
who wants to maintain the status quo.

00:13:49.640 --> 00:13:55.060
That's Joro, who, after accepting Yoki's lunch,
accepted Cosmos' lunch.

00:13:56.140 --> 00:13:57.560
What are you talking about?

00:13:58.100 --> 00:14:02.690
If you accept Yoki's behavior,
which only stems from gratitude,

00:14:02.690 --> 00:14:08.410
you can dodge Cosmos' and my affection,
which comes from another feeling.

00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:10.370
- No...
- But, Joro...

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:12.790
that's not kindness.

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:14.330
It's just running away.

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:16.000
Well, excuse me!

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:17.250
I don't mind.

00:14:17.460 --> 00:14:20.880
I'm also benefiting from your use of that.

00:14:20.880 --> 00:14:22.040
What does that mean?

00:14:23.210 --> 00:14:25.050
Huh, what's that book?

00:14:23.210 --> 00:14:26.510
NATSUME SOUSEKI
HAND-WRITTEN ESSAY
KOKORO

00:14:25.050 --> 00:14:26.510
My treasure.

00:14:27.050 --> 00:14:30.640
I love this book, so I want you to read it.

00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:31.680
Why?

00:14:32.180 --> 00:14:35.890
I want something else we can talk about.
You won't do it?

00:14:37.430 --> 00:14:42.230
I'm not a very fast reader, so I don't know
how long it'll take me to finish it.

00:14:42.610 --> 00:14:47.280
That's fine. When you're finished,
I'd like to know what you thought about it.

00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:53.200
Okay. Also, sorry, but I have something
after school, so I can't come here.

00:14:53.200 --> 00:14:53.990
Something?

00:14:54.580 --> 00:14:56.120
What might that be?

00:14:56.120 --> 00:14:59.580
A long-standing annual tradition.

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:04.340
Thank you! Please come again!

00:15:10.890 --> 00:15:12.220
Joro!

00:15:12.800 --> 00:15:14.140
Found you!

00:15:15.600 --> 00:15:16.930
Ow.

00:15:16.930 --> 00:15:19.190
What are you doing here?

00:15:19.190 --> 00:15:21.810
Isn't there something else
you should say first?

00:15:22.400 --> 00:15:23.440
Oh, right!

00:15:23.440 --> 00:15:25.610
It's almost my birthday!

00:15:25.610 --> 00:15:28.650
Your selfishness knows no bounds!

00:15:28.650 --> 00:15:30.650
Whatever! Just get off me!

00:15:31.860 --> 00:15:33.200
You're mean, Joro!

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:34.070
Sheesh.

00:15:35.030 --> 00:15:37.490
What do I care about your birthday?

00:15:39.410 --> 00:15:40.790
I get it!

00:15:40.790 --> 00:15:43.130
I'm really looking forward to it!

00:15:43.460 --> 00:15:45.000
Were you listening to me?

00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:46.500
Yeah, I was listening!

00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:50.050
- Don't cling to me.
- Okay!

00:15:54.300 --> 00:15:56.470
It's gone! It's gone! It's gone!

00:15:56.970 --> 00:16:00.430
I can't believe I left my bag open!

00:16:00.890 --> 00:16:03.900
Damn it. Did it fall out somewhere?

00:16:04.360 --> 00:16:05.610
But where?

00:16:07.860 --> 00:16:12.780
That ditzy bitch!

00:16:14.240 --> 00:16:16.030
It was right around here.

00:16:16.410 --> 00:16:19.500
Not here. Not here. Why?

00:16:19.500 --> 00:16:22.000
This is where she tackled me.

00:16:19.870 --> 00:16:20.910
Hey.

00:16:22.460 --> 00:16:25.460
It doesn't make sense.
Do I have the wrong place?

00:16:25.830 --> 00:16:28.170
Or maybe I didn't lose it
when she bowled me over?

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:28.170
Hey, you.

00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:32.220
What's wrong?
Looks like you're having some trouble?

00:16:34.010 --> 00:16:35.590
Um, well...

00:16:35.590 --> 00:16:39.350
Hey, Cherry, I want to go home.

00:16:39.350 --> 00:16:41.930
Don't be like that, Tsukimicchi!

00:16:41.930 --> 00:16:44.190
We can't turn our back
when someone's in trouble.

00:16:44.190 --> 00:16:45.150
Uh...

00:16:45.650 --> 00:16:47.820
So what's the problem?

00:16:47.820 --> 00:16:50.570
If we can help you, we will!

00:16:50.570 --> 00:16:52.360
- We?
- We!

00:16:52.700 --> 00:16:56.120
Actually, I'm looking for an important book
I dropped somewhere.

00:16:58.200 --> 00:17:01.700
A book? I see.
Okay, we'll help you search for it!

00:17:01.700 --> 00:17:02.620
But...

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:03.830
We'll help.

00:17:04.120 --> 00:17:05.170
O-Okay.

00:17:05.170 --> 00:17:08.170
We should help with each other's troubles.
Which way did you come from?

00:17:08.170 --> 00:17:10.090
From that shopping mall.

00:17:10.090 --> 00:17:12.670
Then, we'll start looking over there!

00:17:13.470 --> 00:17:15.630
Th-Thank you.

00:17:17.300 --> 00:17:18.600
H-Hi.

00:17:18.890 --> 00:17:20.390
A-Any luck?

00:17:20.390 --> 00:17:22.560
- L-Listen.
- Yes?

00:17:22.810 --> 00:17:26.150
Is the book you're looking for
really important?

00:17:26.150 --> 00:17:28.520
Well, yes. I'd say so.

00:17:28.860 --> 00:17:31.610
I thought so. Oh no.

00:17:33.190 --> 00:17:36.070
Th-That's it! You found it?

00:17:36.320 --> 00:17:38.030
That's great! Thank you!

00:17:39.410 --> 00:17:40.990
Th-That...

00:17:42.200 --> 00:17:45.660
We found it over there, but it was already...

00:17:45.660 --> 00:17:46.920
All beat up.

00:17:46.920 --> 00:17:48.630
Hey, Tsukimicchi!

00:17:48.630 --> 00:17:50.290
Why would it be there?

00:17:50.880 --> 00:17:54.920
B-But, on the bright side,
this kind of gives it character.

00:17:54.920 --> 00:17:55.800
Sorry.

00:17:55.800 --> 00:17:56.800
I'm sorry.

00:17:56.800 --> 00:17:58.090
No, it's okay.

00:17:58.090 --> 00:18:02.220
Please don't apologize.
I'm grateful that you found it.

00:18:04.350 --> 00:18:06.310
I'd better buy a new copy.

00:18:06.730 --> 00:18:10.150
Maybe you don't know what that book is?

00:18:11.270 --> 00:18:15.900
Actually, I know someone
who has that same book.

00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:19.240
I-I asked her how much it was worth.

00:18:22.620 --> 00:18:24.250
Calm down!

00:18:24.250 --> 00:18:29.790
Look! If you consider that it's 1/100,000th
the cost of "Shenmue," it isn't that much!

00:18:30.710 --> 00:18:34.210
It's 1/100,000th the cost of "Shenmue"?

00:18:34.210 --> 00:18:36.380
LET'S MAKE IT TO
KOSHIEN THIS YEAR!

00:18:39.680 --> 00:18:42.720
<i>I'll give you the address
of a bookstore that sells it...</i>

00:18:42.720 --> 00:18:44.390
<i>but don't bite off
more than you can chew.</i>

00:18:44.390 --> 00:18:46.810
<i>Right. Thank you.</i>

00:18:48.640 --> 00:18:50.400
Joro, what are you looking at?

00:18:50.730 --> 00:18:52.060
A part-time job magazine.

00:18:50.730 --> 00:18:53.400
Need a driver's license for this one.
Can't do that.

00:18:52.860 --> 00:18:54.360
Um, Joro?

00:18:53.400 --> 00:18:55.570
Guess all I am qualified for is manual labor.

00:18:54.860 --> 00:18:58.200
Since it's lunchtime, well, here you go.

00:18:55.570 --> 00:18:58.200
If it's a daytime job,
I can only work weekends. So...

00:19:00.490 --> 00:19:02.320
It's a quintuple-decker today!

00:19:02.320 --> 00:19:03.950
One level higher!

00:19:04.200 --> 00:19:06.200
That's breathtaking.

00:19:04.660 --> 00:19:08.910
This one has a high hourly wage,
but no minors! Crap!

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:08.910
- Joro!
- Joro?

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:11.380
H-Hey, Joro!

00:19:11.920 --> 00:19:13.840
Joro is being mean.

00:19:13.840 --> 00:19:17.460
The highest hourly wage is 1,200 yen an hour.
Then, I'll send over a résumé.

00:19:17.460 --> 00:19:18.300
Joro!

00:19:18.800 --> 00:19:19.930
What's the idea, Himawari?

00:19:19.930 --> 00:19:22.760
Stop looking at this! It's time to eat!

00:19:22.760 --> 00:19:24.970
Excuse me? In the first place...

00:19:25.470 --> 00:19:26.350
Wh-What?

00:19:26.640 --> 00:19:28.980
N-Nothing.

00:19:28.980 --> 00:19:33.940
Joro, if you're looking for a part-time job,
why don't you work at my place?

00:19:33.940 --> 00:19:35.360
Your shop, Tsubaki?

00:19:36.030 --> 00:19:38.780
Actually, since we just opened,
we're short-handed.

00:19:38.780 --> 00:19:40.400
Incidentally, what's the hourly pay?

00:19:40.700 --> 00:19:42.820
We pay 1,500 yen an hour.

00:19:44.830 --> 00:19:47.620
I'll do as you order, my angel.

00:19:47.620 --> 00:19:48.790
I mean, my employer.

00:19:48.790 --> 00:19:50.660
I mean, my savior!

00:19:51.040 --> 00:19:54.790
J-Joro, you're a little too close.

00:19:55.000 --> 00:19:58.670
It was fate that you appeared before me.

00:19:58.670 --> 00:20:00.470
Th-Then, that's a yes?

00:20:00.470 --> 00:20:01.430
Of course!

00:20:01.720 --> 00:20:04.390
Joro is drifting away from me.

00:20:04.720 --> 00:20:06.430
All right!

00:20:06.430 --> 00:20:09.270
<i>With this, I've cleared the first obstacle! Next...</i>

00:20:09.270 --> 00:20:13.400
Then, I guess you can't come
to the library after school anymore?

00:20:14.230 --> 00:20:15.810
I-I suppose not.

00:20:15.810 --> 00:20:18.900
I won't be able to come
until I save up the amount I need.

00:20:18.900 --> 00:20:20.070
I'll miss you.

00:20:20.360 --> 00:20:22.400
L-Listen, Pansy.

00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:23.660
Yes?

00:20:23.660 --> 00:20:25.910
Um, I have something to tell you.

00:20:25.910 --> 00:20:28.410
Do you have a few minutes
during the next break?

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:32.500
Yes. Sure.

00:20:33.870 --> 00:20:34.710
I'm sorry!

00:20:36.250 --> 00:20:37.170
Um...

00:20:37.460 --> 00:20:40.590
because of my carelessness,
the book I borrowed from you was ruined.

00:20:41.670 --> 00:20:46.010
So I'm going to work and save up money
until I have enough to buy you another copy.

00:20:46.220 --> 00:20:48.470
Until then, I can't go to the library after school.

00:20:48.890 --> 00:20:50.060
I don't need it.

00:20:50.060 --> 00:20:51.890
I-I have to do this!

00:20:52.310 --> 00:20:56.860
It's fine. It's really unfortunate,
but what's done is done.

00:20:57.480 --> 00:21:00.070
I'm so sorry! I, uh...

00:21:00.440 --> 00:21:02.740
If there's anything I can do for you, I'll do it!

00:21:02.740 --> 00:21:06.910
Then, instead of working part-time,
I'd like you to come to the library after school.

00:21:06.910 --> 00:21:07.910
I can't do that.

00:21:07.910 --> 00:21:09.740
I told you I don't need another copy.

00:21:09.740 --> 00:21:11.580
I'm saying you do.

00:21:14.290 --> 00:21:15.960
Oh. And so?

00:21:16.170 --> 00:21:18.380
What are you going to do
with that battered book?

00:21:18.380 --> 00:21:20.300
Let me hold on to it for a while longer.

00:21:20.300 --> 00:21:21.510
Why?

00:21:21.510 --> 00:21:24.300
- Because I haven't finished reading it.
- Oh.

00:21:24.970 --> 00:21:28.890
Just when I think you're only being selfish,
you show a flash of kindness.

00:21:29.890 --> 00:21:32.140
That's me all over.

00:21:32.140 --> 00:21:34.060
We're done here, aren't we?

00:21:34.060 --> 00:21:37.310
Then, I'll see you later, obstinate Joro.

00:21:42.990 --> 00:21:45.610
<i>I have to do this!</i>

00:21:47.410 --> 00:21:49.870
CHEERFUL SKEWERS

00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:49.870
Are you ready?

00:21:50.120 --> 00:21:51.540
I-I hope so.

00:21:52.370 --> 00:21:53.950
It looks good on you.

00:21:53.950 --> 00:21:57.460
I may make a lot of mistakes,
but I'm counting on your help.

00:21:57.460 --> 00:21:58.750
And I'm counting on you!

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:04.800
This is where the true payback begins.

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:39.980
EPISODE 09
MY CONCLUSION
AFTER MUCH CONSIDERATION

00:23:36.310 --> 00:23:38.560
My Conclusion After Much Consideration
